hadiths[12]{hadithnumber,text}:
"23269","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: Husayn narrated to us: Abu Nahik narrated to me: Abu Zayd Amr ibn Akhtab al-Ansari narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked for water, so I brought him a cup containing water, and in it was a hair, so I removed it. He said: O Allah, beautify him. He said: I saw him when he was ninety-four years old, with not a white hair in his beard."
"23270","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Nahik saying: I heard Abu Zayd Amr ibn Akhtab saying: I saw the seal between the shoulders of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), like a man, he said with his three fingers thus, and I wiped it with my hand."
"23271","Ali ibn al-Hasan, meaning Ibn Shaqiq, narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me: Abu Nahik al-Azdi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Akhtab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked for water, so I brought him a vessel containing water, and in it was a hair. I lifted it, then handed it to him. He said: O Allah, beautify him. He said: I saw him after ninety-three years, with not a white hair in his head and beard."
"23272","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: Tamim ibn Huways narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Zayd saying: I fought alongside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) thirteen times. Shu'bah said: And he is the grandfather of Azzah, this one."
"23273","Hajjaj ibn Nusayr al-Fasatitiyy narrated to us, he said, and I heard nothing from him besides it, he said: Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin: Abu Zayd ibn Akhtab narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: May Allah beautify you. Anas said: And he was a handsome man of good bearing."
"23274","Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Khalid informed us, from Abu Qilabah, from a man of his people, Khalid said: I think him Amr ibn Bujdan, from Abu Zayd al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed between the houses of the Ansar and found a smell of cooking. He said: Who made this, or as he said, Isma'il doubted. A man came out and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is a day in which meat is disliked, and I hastened my sacrifice. He said: Repeat it. He said: By Allah, I have nothing but a jadh' or a lamb of sheep. He said: Slaughter it, and no jadh' will suffice for anyone after you."
"23275","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us: Abu Qilabah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Bujdan, from Abu Zayd al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed among our dwellings, and he mentioned its meaning."
"23276","Abu Asim narrated to us: Azzah ibn Thabit narrated to us: Ilba' ibn Ahmar al-Yashkuri narrated to us: Abu Zayd al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in Fajr prayer, then ascended the minbar and addressed us until Zuhr came. Then he descended and prayed Zuhr, then ascended the minbar and addressed us until Asr came. Then he descended and prayed Asr, then ascended the minbar and addressed us until the sun set. He told us of what was and what will be. The most knowledgeable of us is the most retentive of us."
"23277","Abu Asim narrated to us: Azzah narrated to us: Ilba' ibn Ahmar narrated to us: Abu Zayd narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abu Zayd, come near me and wipe my back. He uncovered his back, so I wiped his back and placed the seal between my fingers. He said: I pressed it. It was said: What is the seal? He said: Hair gathered upon his shoulder."
"23278","Abu Asim narrated to us: Azzah ibn Thabit narrated to us: Ilba' ibn Ahmar narrated to us: Abu Zayd narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped his face and prayed for him for beauty. He said: More than one informed me that he reached a hundred and some years, black of head and beard, except for a few white hairs on his head."
"23279","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Zayd al-Ansari, that a man freed six slaves at his death, having no wealth besides them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots between them, so he freed two and kept four enslaved."
"23280","Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Khalid informed us: Abu Qilabah narrated to us, from Abu Zayd al-Ansari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of that, meaning the like of the hadith of Mansur from al-Hasan, that a man freed six owned slaves of his, and he said in it: He cast lots between them."
